; Hand-authored array-content recoverability fixture (P1-a shot-①b MECHANISM test).
; NAMED state FFs (busy/key/mem) + DIRECT mem[key] read (no yosys reset-mux/observable
; artifacts), so the reset-cube gate pins every register and the ONLY hard axis is the
; in-cone array content. Recovery: busy -> 0 iff mem[key] == all-ones(3); mem is freely
; env-writable (mem[waddr]=wdata), so from any busy state the env can write mem[key]=3
; and recover -> AG EF(busy==0) HOLDS. The array is in-cone, so the exact ROBDD SKIPs and
; the property falls to the predicate cube; the deciding predicate is the Select mem[key]==3.
1 sort bitvec 1
2 sort bitvec 2
3 sort array 2 2
; inputs (free environment)
4 input 1 start
5 input 2 waddr
6 input 2 wdata
; state cells (named -> pinned in init_values; init 0)
7 state 1 busy
8 state 2 key
9 state 3 mem
10 const 1 0
11 init 1 7 10
12 const 2 00
13 init 2 8 12
14 const 2 11
; recovery guard: mem[key] == 3
15 read 2 9 8
16 eq 1 15 14
; control: busy' = (start & !busy) ? 1 : ((busy & mem[key]==3) ? 0 : busy)
17 not 1 7
18 and 1 4 17
19 const 1 1
20 and 1 7 16
21 ite 1 20 10 7
22 ite 1 18 19 21
23 next 1 7 22
; key' = (start & !busy) ? waddr : key
24 ite 2 18 5 8
25 next 2 8 24
; mem' = write(mem, waddr, wdata)  (freely env-writable)
26 write 3 9 5 6
27 next 3 9 26
